WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.060
These theoretical nodes must also be
reflected in the physical culture of the

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:08.260
research environment. Institutions are
mandated to engineer cultures that

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.900
promote equity, diversity, and inclusion,
alongside mutual respect.

4
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.400
The use of artificial intelligence and
automated tools must comply with the

5
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.520
established standards and norms of the
relevant discipline.

6
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.680
All research must be performed according
to strict legal provisions and

7
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.180
ethical principles that protect research
participants and subjects.

8
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:33.180
Boundary spanning initiatives, including
citizen science, require rigorous

9
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.600
oversight, training, and safeguards.

10
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:40.020
The ethical framework is functional when
manifesting as measurable safeguards

11
00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.360
and inclusive practices in the laboratory.
